@startuml host-provider-lifecycle
' Abstract lifecycle of the stable VtResource boundary. Sources:
' vinary-tree-interop/include/vinary_tree_interop.h and
' proofs/tla/HostProviderLifecycle.tla.
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #455A64
  LifeLineBorderColor #455A64
  GroupBorderColor #455A64
  GroupBackgroundColor #ECEFF1
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #E3F2FD
  BorderColor #1565C0
}

title <b>Host-provider resource lifecycle</b>\n<size:11><i>one owned base resource, one retained snapshot, optional token or cursor</i></size>

participant "Caller" as Caller #ECEFF1
participant "Consumer\nvalidation and admission" as Consumer #FCF3CF
participant "Context gate\nby opaque identity" as Gate #C5E1A5
box "Foreign provider — trust boundary" #FFCDD2
  participant "VtResource\nbase vtable" as Base #FFCDD2
  participant "Optional interface\nWFST / algebra / entries" as Interface #FFCDD2
end box

Caller -> Consumer : pass owned VtResource
Consumer -> Base : validate size, ABI version, required callbacks
Consumer -> Base : retain(context)
note right of Consumer : A retained owner keeps context live;\nfinalizer and explicit close use the same release law.
Consumer -> Gate : acquire context-identity bootstrap gate
Gate -> Base : query_interface(id, minimum_version, &out)
Base --> Gate : raw status and optional interface pointer
Gate --> Consumer : validated capability or Unsupported
note right of Gate : A failed negotiation publishes no output.\nBootstrap discovery is serialized before flags are known.

alt supported snapshot capability
  Consumer -> Interface : snapshot(context, &snapshot)
  Interface --> Consumer : one owned immutable snapshot
  Consumer -> Gate : share gate if context aliases base
  Consumer -> Base : release(base context)
  note right of Consumer : Snapshot retains its own identity;\nbase may close without invalidating it.
  alt scalar-WFST callbacks
    Caller -> Consumer : request state or bounded arc page
    Consumer -> Gate : enter serial gate, or validate parallel claim
    Gate -> Interface : callback(snapshot context)
    Interface --> Gate : raw status, written count, total count
    Gate --> Consumer : release admission on return or unwind
    Consumer --> Caller : validated page or explicit error status
  else dynamic algebra token
    Consumer -> Interface : create token in retained context
    Interface --> Consumer : slot and generation
    Consumer -> Interface : use / clone / release owned token
    Interface --> Consumer : reject stale generation or wrong context
  else dictionary entry cursor
    Consumer -> Interface : open(snapshot), next_batch(capacity)
    Interface --> Consumer : one generation-tagged batch lease
    Consumer -> Interface : release_batch(generation)
    Consumer -> Interface : cancel or close cursor
  end
  Consumer -> Base : release(snapshot context) after all users settle
end

legend right
  |<#FCF3CF> Consumer validation and callback policy |
  |<#C5E1A5> Context gate for admission |
  |<#FFCDD2> Foreign provider, whose replies require validation |
  |<#ECEFF1> Calling application |
endlegend
@enduml
